<component><section><templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.17" extension="2015-08-01"/><code code="29762-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Social history Narrative"/><title>Social History</title><text><list><item>A Hindu monk of a monastic order, under vows of renunciation and celibacy; head of the order and of its service mission; lives at the order&apos;s monastery by the river with his brother monks and young disciples; teaches daily classes on scripture and lectures widely [S]</item><item>Daily routine: rises before dawn for meditation and worship; teaching and correspondence through the day; often works late into the night. Travels often, in India and abroad, and is now planning a long journey in the mountains from the spring [S]</item><item>Diet: eats with the monastery, mostly vegetarian (rice, chapati, dal, vegetables, milk and yogurt, and sweets offered after worship), with fish at some meals by his own choice; keeps religious fasts on the eleventh day of each lunar fortnight and at major festivals, sometimes without water. A year ago he believed that eating only meat and drinking no water was the way to live with diabetes [S]</item><item>No alcohol, by his vows; no tobacco use now; no drug use. Incense and smoke from the monastery kitchen fires [S]</item><item>Supports: his brother monks and disciples, who share his daily life; his faith and practice. He wants his care to fit his vows and his duties, and he alone decides it [S]</item></list></text></section></component>

